    provider_query_result_v2_wire_codec_missing_2026-09-13, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: doc item-4 digest helpers and the 84-byte V1 world were already landed (the doc's 60-byte u64 world was superseded by a main-line transplant); built V2 on the landed V1. Added SimpleProviderQueryResultV2 (base + abi_digest_256) and SIZE=116 in src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/composition/provider_contract.spl; encode/decode_provider_query_result_v2 + ProviderQueryWireResultReadV2 in src/os/smf/provider_query_wire.spl (V1 codec owns its bytes so offsets cannot drift; digest words per abi_digest.spl frozen order; inherits all V1 validation). New spec test/01_unit/os/smf/provider_query_result_v2_wire_spec.spl 8/8 PASS (verbatim-prefix equality, BE offsets, round trip, V1-view decode, zero-tail undeclared, size rejection, inherited validation, encode passthrough). Repaired stale acceptance evidence: provider_abi_digest_admission_spec now builds a real digest (11/11; 60-byte title corrected to 84); provider_query_wire_spec repinned from the abandoned u64-era offsets (4/4 - it was already red at HEAD; my wire diff is purely additive, verified via git diff). Neighbours provider_loader 12/12, vector_call 4/4, query_call 2/2, native_provider_v1 1/1, bootstrap_driver_client 9/9, cli_registry 5/5 PASS. Residual: compiler_driver_provider_v1 1/5 needs ELF objects (Windows host emits COFF) - environmental; two pre-existing visibility warnings untouched. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/os/smf/provider_query_result_v2_wire_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/os/smf/provider_query_wire_spec.spl"

